<title>POLAND: Poland to raise barley import duty to 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Poland to raise barley import duty to 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will increase import duties on barley to 20 percent from the present 10 percent on June 1, the agriculture minister said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;From June 1, we will return to 20 percent duties on barley,&quot; Jaroslaw Kalinowski told reporters after a cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>Poland reduced tariffs on most grains to zero last year as part of an anti-inflationary package before raising them to 10 percent in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Tariffs for most grains are due to return to the previous level of 20 percent as of July 1, 1997.</p>
<p>--Robert Bogdanski, Warsaw newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
